  },
  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 21 May 1952 and declared by Geo. McGowan, returning officer, on Thursday 22 May. The three aldermen elected in 1947 and all twelve councillors were due for election. Labels as printed: Offl. U. official Unionist, U Unionist, Ex-Ser. ex-serviceman, Trades C. Mid-Ulster Trades Council. Councillors: H. McCourt, an ex-serviceman at his first attempt, headed the list; T. Newell became the first Mid-Ulster Trades Council representative on the council. Total votes cast 4,531; 69 per cent of the electorate; 203 spoilt."
}
